      "Set \"Advertised power rate\" to the headline price in your contract, in dollars per kilowatt-hour. The slider moves in steps of $0.001 per kilowatt-hour, a tenth of a cent, and stops at $0.20 per kilowatt-hour. Now add the two extras the host puts on your bill: \"Management fee\" and \"Power factor extra\". You type both in as a percentage of your power bill.",
