        whereToFind: "The pricing schedule of your hosting agreement, usually on page one or two. Then check it against reality. Take last month's invoice. Find the power or energy line. Divide the dollars by the kilowatt-hours on that same invoice. If the answer is not the rate in your contract, the difference is one of the other sliders below. If your rate is above $0.200 per kilowatt-hour the slider will not reach it. Enter half your rate and double every dollar figure the tool hands back — the effective rate, the after-fees row and the after-lost-hours row all scale straight up, and the percentage above the advertised rate does not change at all. The tool does not care which currency the numbers are in, as long as both contracts you are comparing are in the same one.",
